§§ `s 8A, s 36, Act s 7(8), (9) -- the firefighter presumption`

-- An Act item (brain cancer, 5 years): at the period, and just under it.
#ASSERT `Is my firefighting employment presumed to have contributed to my disease?` `primary site brain cancer` 5 TRUE TRUE TRUE (`on` 1 1 2020) (`on` 1 6 2020) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my firefighting employment presumed to have contributed to my disease?` `primary site brain cancer` 4.99 TRUE TRUE TRUE (`on` 1 1 2020) (`on` 1 6 2020) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An Act item is not touched by reg s 36, but s 7(8) commenced on 7 December 2011 (endnote 3 of the Act) and the
-- amending Act's application provision is not deposited (fork F15): sustained in 2005, or decided in 2010, no answer.
#ASSERT `Is my firefighting employment presumed to have contributed to my disease?` `primary site bladder cancer` 15 TRUE TRUE TRUE (`on` 1 1 2005) (`on` 1 6 2010) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is my firefighting employment presumed to have contributed to my disease?` `primary site bladder cancer` 15 TRUE TRUE TRUE (`on` 1 1 2005) (`on` 1 6 2015) EQUALS NOTHING
-- An Act item sustained after 4 July 2011 and decided before 17 December 2022: reg s 36 does not reach it.
#ASSERT `Is my firefighting employment presumed to have contributed to my disease?` `primary site bladder cancer` 15 TRUE TRUE TRUE (`on` 1 8 2011) (`on` 1 6 2015) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my firefighting employment presumed to have contributed to my disease?` `primary site bladder cancer` 14.5 TRUE TRUE TRUE (`on` 1 8 2011) (`on` 1 6 2015) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Commencement edges: decided on 6 and 7 December 2011; sustained on 3 and 4 July 2011.
#ASSERT `Is my firefighting employment presumed to have contributed to my disease?` `primary site brain cancer` 5 TRUE TRUE TRUE (`on` 1 8 2011) (`on` 6 12 2011) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is my firefighting employment presumed to have contributed to my disease?` `primary site brain cancer` 5 TRUE TRUE TRUE (`on` 1 8 2011) (`on` 7 12 2011) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my firefighting employment presumed to have contributed to my disease?` `primary site brain cancer` 5 TRUE TRUE TRUE (`on` 3 7 2011) (`on` 1 6 2015) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is my firefighting employment presumed to have contributed to my disease?` `primary site brain cancer` 5 TRUE TRUE TRUE (`on` 4 7 2011) (`on` 1 6 2015) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 7(9)(a): the relevant authority is not satisfied the duties were a not insubstantial portion (fork F16).
#ASSERT `Is my firefighting employment presumed to have contributed to my disease?` `primary site brain cancer` 20 FALSE TRUE TRUE (`on` 1 1 2020) (`on` 1 6 2020) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A prescribed cancer (lung, 15 years), sustained after 4 July 2011 and decided after 17 December 2022.
#ASSERT `Is my firefighting employment presumed to have contributed to my disease?` `primary site lung cancer` 15 TRUE TRUE TRUE (`on` 1 5 2015) (`on` 10 1 2023) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my firefighting employment presumed to have contributed to my disease?` `primary site lung cancer` 14 TRUE TRUE TRUE (`on` 1 5 2015) (`on` 10 1 2023) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Reg s 36 edges: sustained on 3 and 4 July 2011; decided on 16 and 17 December 2022.
#ASSERT `Is my firefighting employment presumed to have contributed to my disease?` `primary site lung cancer` 15 TRUE TRUE TRUE (`on` 3 7 2011) (`on` 10 1 2023) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is my firefighting employment presumed to have contributed to my disease?` `primary site lung cancer` 15 TRUE TRUE TRUE (`on` 4 7 2011) (`on` 10 1 2023) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my firefighting employment presumed to have contributed to my disease?` `primary site lung cancer` 15 TRUE TRUE TRUE (`on` 1 5 2015) (`on` 16 12 2022) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Is my firefighting employment presumed to have contributed to my disease?` `primary site lung cancer` 15 TRUE TRUE TRUE (`on` 1 5 2015) (`on` 17 12 2022) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Ten-year prescribed cancers, at and under the period.
#ASSERT `Is my firefighting employment presumed to have contributed to my disease?` `primary site cervical cancer` 10 TRUE TRUE TRUE (`on` 1 3 2020) (`on` 1 3 2024) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my firefighting employment presumed to have contributed to my disease?` `primary site cervical cancer` 9.9 TRUE TRUE TRUE (`on` 1 3 2020) (`on` 1 3 2024) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Is my firefighting employment presumed to have contributed to my disease?` `malignant mesothelioma` 15 TRUE TRUE TRUE (`on` 1 3 2020) (`on` 1 3 2024) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 7(9)(c): firefighting for another employer (a State fire service) does not count.
#ASSERT `Is my firefighting employment presumed to have contributed to my disease?` `primary site brain cancer` 20 TRUE FALSE TRUE (`on` 1 1 2020) (`on` 1 6 2020) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 7(8)(c): no exposure to the hazards of a fire scene.
#ASSERT `Is my firefighting employment presumed to have contributed to my disease?` `primary site brain cancer` 20 TRUE TRUE FALSE (`on` 1 1 2020) (`on` 1 6 2020) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 7(8)(a): a disease not in the table.
#ASSERT `Is my firefighting employment presumed to have contributed to my disease?` `another disease` 30 TRUE TRUE TRUE (`on` 1 1 2020) (`on` 1 6 2020) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Act s 8(9B), (9E) -- which indexation`

-- Ceased, no other change in the 12 months: both subsections read on (finding 3).
#ASSERT `Which indexation applies to my normal weekly earnings?` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `both s 8(9B) and s 8(9E) on the words of the Act`
#ASSERT `Which indexation applies to my normal weekly earnings?` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 8(9B) and regulations ss 8 and 9 (after leaving Commonwealth employment)`
#ASSERT `Which indexation applies to my normal weekly earnings?` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `s 8(9B) and regulations ss 8 and 9 (after leaving Commonwealth employment)`
#ASSERT `Which indexation applies to my normal weekly earnings?` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 8(9E) and regulations ss 10 and 11 (no other change in 12 months)`
#ASSERT `Which indexation applies to my normal weekly earnings?` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `neither`
#ASSERT `Which indexation applies to my normal weekly earnings?` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `neither`

§§ `Act s 8(9C) -- the first indexation date`

#ASSERT `When are my normal weekly earnings first indexed after I stopped working?` (`on` 31 3 2025) EQUALS `on` 1 7 2025
#ASSERT `When are my normal weekly earnings first indexed after I stopped working?` (`on` 30 6 2025) EQUALS `on` 1 7 2025
#ASSERT `When are my normal weekly earnings first indexed after I stopped working?` (`on` 1 7 2025) EQUALS `on` 1 7 2026
#ASSERT `When are my normal weekly earnings first indexed after I stopped working?` (`on` 31 12 2025) EQUALS `on` 1 7 2026

§§ `regs ss 9, 11 -- F and the increase`

-- 105 / 102 = 1.029411...; to 4 places 1.0294; rounded up to 3 places 1.030.
#ASSERT `What is the indexation factor this 1 July?` 105 102 EQUALS 1.03
-- 102 / 100 = 1.0200: nothing to round; 1.020.
#ASSERT `What is the indexation factor this 1 July?` 102 100 EQUALS 1.02
-- 102.01 / 100 = 1.0201: rounded up to 1.021.
#ASSERT `What is the indexation factor this 1 July?` 102.01 100 EQUALS 1.021
-- 102.009 / 100 = 1.02009: to 4 places 1.0200 (the fifth place is cut off), so 1.020.
#ASSERT `What is the indexation factor this 1 July?` 102.009 100 EQUALS 1.02
-- No rise, and a fall: F is 1.000 (the greater of the two).
#ASSERT `What is the indexation factor this 1 July?` 100 100 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `What is the indexation factor this 1 July?` 99 100 EQUALS 1
-- WE $1,000, F 1.030: 1,000 x 0.030 = $30.00.
#ASSERT `How much do my normal weekly earnings go up on 1 July?` 1000 105 102 EQUALS 30
-- WE $1,234.56, F 1.030: 37.0368; to 3 places 37.036; rounded up to 2 places $37.04.
#ASSERT `How much do my normal weekly earnings go up on 1 July?` 1234.56 105 102 EQUALS 37.04
-- WE $850, F 1.020: $17.00; F 1.021: 850 x 0.021 = $17.85.
#ASSERT `How much do my normal weekly earnings go up on 1 July?` 850 102 100 EQUALS 17
#ASSERT `How much do my normal weekly earnings go up on 1 July?` 850 102.01 100 EQUALS 17.85
-- No rise, and a fall: no increase.
#ASSERT `How much do my normal weekly earnings go up on 1 July?` 850 100 100 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `How much do my normal weekly earnings go up on 1 July?` 850 99 100 EQUALS 0

§§ `reg s 11A(1) -- the last day for determining my claim`

-- Received 1 April 2024 (the first day s 11A applies, s 37): an injury, 20 days counting 1 April, so 20 April 2024.
#ASSERT `By what day must my claim be determined?` `an injury other than a disease, or its aggravation` (`on` 1 4 2024) TRUE `no pauses` EQUALS JUST (`on` 20 4 2024)
-- A disease, 60 days: 1 April + 59 = 30 May 2024.
#ASSERT `By what day must my claim be determined?` `a disease, or its aggravation` (`on` 1 4 2024) TRUE `no pauses` EQUALS JUST (`on` 30 5 2024)
-- Received 31 March 2024: before s 37's start, no prescribed period.
#ASSERT `By what day must my claim be determined?` `an injury other than a disease, or its aggravation` (`on` 31 3 2024) TRUE `no pauses` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not made in accordance with s 54: the period does not start.
#ASSERT `By what day must my claim be determined?` `an injury other than a disease, or its aggravation` (`on` 1 5 2024) FALSE `no pauses` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Received 1 May 2024, no pause: 20 May. A pause of 5 to 9 May (5 days, both ends counted out): 25 May.
#ASSERT `By what day must my claim be determined?` `an injury other than a disease, or its aggravation` (`on` 1 5 2024) TRUE `no pauses` EQUALS JUST (`on` 20 5 2024)
#ASSERT `By what day must my claim be determined?` `an injury other than a disease, or its aggravation` (`on` 1 5 2024) TRUE (LIST (`a pause from` 5 5 2024 `to` 9 5 2024)) EQUALS JUST (`on` 25 5 2024)
-- A pause from 28 April to 1 May covers the day of receipt: the count starts on 2 May, so 21 May.
#ASSERT `By what day must my claim be determined?` `an injury other than a disease, or its aggravation` (`on` 1 5 2024) TRUE (LIST (`a pause from` 28 4 2024 `to` 1 5 2024)) EQUALS JUST (`on` 21 5 2024)
-- Overlapping pauses 5-9 May and 8-12 May cover 5 to 12 May, 8 days, not 10: 28 May.
#ASSERT `By what day must my claim be determined?` `an injury other than a disease, or its aggravation` (`on` 1 5 2024) TRUE (LIST (`a pause from` 5 5 2024 `to` 9 5 2024), (`a pause from` 8 5 2024 `to` 12 5 2024)) EQUALS JUST (`on` 28 5 2024)
-- A pause wholly after the last day changes nothing; a pause on the last day itself moves it a day.
#ASSERT `By what day must my claim be determined?` `an injury other than a disease, or its aggravation` (`on` 1 5 2024) TRUE (LIST (`a pause from` 1 6 2024 `to` 10 6 2024)) EQUALS JUST (`on` 20 5 2024)
#ASSERT `By what day must my claim be determined?` `an injury other than a disease, or its aggravation` (`on` 1 5 2024) TRUE (LIST (`a pause from` 20 5 2024 `to` 20 5 2024)) EQUALS JUST (`on` 21 5 2024)
-- A disease claim with a 14-day examination pause, 10 to 23 June 2024: received 1 June, 60 days would end 30 July; plus 14: 13 August.
#ASSERT `By what day must my claim be determined?` `a disease, or its aggravation` (`on` 1 6 2024) TRUE (LIST (`a pause from` 10 6 2024 `to` 23 6 2024)) EQUALS JUST (`on` 13 8 2024)

§§ `Act s 61(1A) -- was my claim determined in time (regulative rule)`

-- Received 1 May 2024, injury, no pause, last day 20 May.
#ASSERT `Was my claim determined in time?` `an injury other than a disease, or its aggravation` (`on` 1 5 2024) TRUE TRUE (`on` 20 5 2024) (`on` 1 7 2024) `no pauses` EQUALS JUST `decided within the period`
#ASSERT `Was my claim determined in time?` `an injury other than a disease, or its aggravation` (`on` 1 5 2024) TRUE TRUE (`on` 21 5 2024) (`on` 1 7 2024) `no pauses` EQUALS JUST `decided after the period ended`
#ASSERT `Was my claim determined in time?` `an injury other than a disease, or its aggravation` (`on` 1 5 2024) TRUE TRUE (`on` 1 5 2024) (`on` 1 7 2024) `no pauses` EQUALS JUST `decided within the period`
#ASSERT `Was my claim determined in time?` `an injury other than a disease, or its aggravation` (`on` 1 5 2024) TRUE FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) (`on` 20 5 2024) `no pauses` EQUALS JUST `not yet decided, and the period has not ended`
#ASSERT `Was my claim determined in time?` `an injury other than a disease, or its aggravation` (`on` 1 5 2024) TRUE FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) (`on` 21 5 2024) `no pauses` EQUALS JUST `not yet decided, and the period has ended`
-- With the 5-9 May pause the last day is 25 May.
#ASSERT `Was my claim determined in time?` `an injury other than a disease, or its aggravation` (`on` 1 5 2024) TRUE TRUE (`on` 25 5 2024) (`on` 1 7 2024) (LIST (`a pause from` 5 5 2024 `to` 9 5 2024)) EQUALS JUST `decided within the period`
#ASSERT `Was my claim determined in time?` `an injury other than a disease, or its aggravation` (`on` 1 5 2024) TRUE TRUE (`on` 26 5 2024) (`on` 1 7 2024) (LIST (`a pause from` 5 5 2024 `to` 9 5 2024)) EQUALS JUST `decided after the period ended`
-- A disease claim received 1 April 2024: last day 30 May.
#ASSERT `Was my claim determined in time?` `a disease, or its aggravation` (`on` 1 4 2024) TRUE TRUE (`on` 30 5 2024) (`on` 1 7 2024) `no pauses` EQUALS JUST `decided within the period`
#ASSERT `Was my claim determined in time?` `a disease, or its aggravation` (`on` 1 4 2024) TRUE TRUE (`on` 31 5 2024) (`on` 1 7 2024) `no pauses` EQUALS JUST `decided after the period ended`
-- A claim received before 1 April 2024: no prescribed period.
#ASSERT `Was my claim determined in time?` `an injury other than a disease, or its aggravation` (`on` 1 3 2024) TRUE TRUE (`on` 1 6 2024) (`on` 1 7 2024) `no pauses` EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `reg s 11A(2), Act s 62(6) -- my request for reconsideration`

-- 30 calendar days counting the day of receipt: 1 April 2024 to 30 April 2024; 15 December 2024 to 13 January 2025.
#ASSERT `By what day must my request for reconsideration be decided?` `reconsideration of a determination on my claim (Act s 62)` (`on` 1 4 2024) EQUALS JUST (`on` 30 4 2024)
#ASSERT `By what day must my request for reconsideration be decided?` `reconsideration of a determination on my claim (Act s 62)` (`on` 15 12 2024) EQUALS JUST (`on` 13 1 2025)
#ASSERT `By what day must my request for reconsideration be decided?` `reconsideration of a determination on my claim (Act s 62)` (`on` 31 3 2024) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `By what day must my request for reconsideration be decided?` `reconsideration of a rehabilitation determination (Act s 38)` (`on` 1 4 2024) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Was my request for reconsideration decided in time?` `reconsideration of a determination on my claim (Act s 62)` (`on` 1 4 2024) TRUE (`on` 30 4 2024) (`on` 1 7 2024) EQUALS JUST `decided within the period`
#ASSERT `Was my request for reconsideration decided in time?` `reconsideration of a determination on my claim (Act s 62)` (`on` 1 4 2024) TRUE (`on` 1 5 2024) (`on` 1 7 2024) EQUALS JUST `decided after the period ended`
#ASSERT `Was my request for reconsideration decided in time?` `reconsideration of a determination on my claim (Act s 62)` (`on` 1 4 2024) FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) (`on` 30 4 2024) EQUALS JUST `not yet decided, and the period has not ended`
#ASSERT `Was my request for reconsideration decided in time?` `reconsideration of a determination on my claim (Act s 62)` (`on` 1 4 2024) FALSE (`on` 1 1 2000) (`on` 1 5 2024) EQUALS JUST `not yet decided, and the period has ended`
#ASSERT `Was my request for reconsideration decided in time?` `reconsideration of a rehabilitation determination (Act s 38)` (`on` 1 4 2024) TRUE (`on` 2 4 2024) (`on` 1 7 2024) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `regs ss 19, 21, 27, 28 -- who is liable`

#ASSERT `Who is liable for my compensation after my employer's licence changed?` `a Commonwealth authority (licensed authority)` `suspended` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `my employer, and Comcare may pay it during the suspension`
#ASSERT `Who is liable for my compensation after my employer's licence changed?` `a Commonwealth authority (licensed authority)` `suspended` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Who is liable for my compensation after my employer's licence changed?` `a Commonwealth authority (licensed authority)` `revoked` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `my former employer, and Comcare may pay it`
#ASSERT `Who is liable for my compensation after my employer's licence changed?` `a Commonwealth authority (licensed authority)` `revoked` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `Comcare`
#ASSERT `Who is liable for my compensation after my employer's licence changed?` `a Commonwealth authority (licensed authority)` `revoked` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `Comcare`
#ASSERT `Who is liable for my compensation after my employer's licence changed?` `a Commonwealth authority (licensed authority)` `revoked` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Who is liable for my compensation after my employer's licence changed?` `a corporation (licensed corporation)` `suspended` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Who is liable for my compensation after my employer's licence changed?` `a corporation (licensed corporation)` `revoked` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `my former employer`
#ASSERT `Who is liable for my compensation after my employer's licence changed?` `a corporation (licensed corporation)` `revoked` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `no one under the Act, which has ceased to apply`
#ASSERT `Who is liable for my compensation after my employer's licence changed?` `a corporation (licensed corporation)` `revoked` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `regs ss 19, 21, 27, 30 -- who manages my claim`

#ASSERT `Who manages my claim after my employer's licence changed?` `a Commonwealth authority (licensed authority)` `suspended` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `Comcare, in my employer's name, during the suspension`
#ASSERT `Who manages my claim after my employer's licence changed?` `a Commonwealth authority (licensed authority)` `suspended` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Who manages my claim after my employer's licence changed?` `a Commonwealth authority (licensed authority)` `revoked` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `Comcare`
#ASSERT `Who manages my claim after my employer's licence changed?` `a Commonwealth authority (licensed authority)` `revoked` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `Comcare`
#ASSERT `Who manages my claim after my employer's licence changed?` `a corporation (licensed corporation)` `revoked` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `my former employer, as if the licence had not been revoked`
#ASSERT `Who manages my claim after my employer's licence changed?` `a corporation (licensed corporation)` `revoked` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `Comcare, or a person Comcare arranges`
#ASSERT `Who manages my claim after my employer's licence changed?` `a corporation (licensed corporation)` `revoked` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST `not my former employer, and the Act has ceased to apply`
#ASSERT `Who manages my claim after my employer's licence changed?` `a corporation (licensed corporation)` `suspended` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Who manages my claim after my employer's licence changed?` `a corporation (licensed corporation)` `revoked` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `regs ss 19, 21, 30 -- passing my claim to Comcare`

#ASSERT `Must my employer pass my claim to Comcare?` `a Commonwealth authority (licensed authority)` `suspended` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must my employer pass my claim to Comcare?` `a Commonwealth authority (licensed authority)` `revoked` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must my employer pass my claim to Comcare?` `a Commonwealth authority (licensed authority)` `revoked` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Must my employer pass my claim to Comcare?` `a corporation (licensed corporation)` `revoked` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Must my employer pass my claim to Comcare?` `a corporation (licensed corporation)` `revoked` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Must my employer pass my claim to Comcare?` `a corporation (licensed corporation)` `revoked` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Must my employer pass my claim to Comcare?` `a corporation (licensed corporation)` `suspended` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `regs ss 22, 25, 28, 31 -- my rehabilitation authority`

#ASSERT `Who is my rehabilitation authority after the licence was revoked?` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST `the principal officer of my former employer`
#ASSERT `Who is my rehabilitation authority after the licence was revoked?` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the person Comcare has arranged`
#ASSERT `Who is my rehabilitation authority after the licence was revoked?` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST `the person Comcare has arranged`
#ASSERT `Who is my rehabilitation authority after the licence was revoked?` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
